---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Why it matters" description="Real understanding means going deeper than polls or party lines. Our mission is to listen to people as they really are.">

  <section class="container-site pt-14 md:pt-20 pb-10">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Our Mission</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-[clamp(2.25rem,5vw,4rem)] leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.02em] max-w-4xl">
      Real understanding begins with <em>listening</em>.
    </h1>
    <p class="prose-body mt-6 max-w-2xl">
      We listen to people as they really are &mdash; complex, evolving, and often beyond simple labels.
      And we do it because understanding people is the first step toward building a better future.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container-site pb-10">
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 md:gap-14">

      <article class="p-8 md:p-10 rounded-2xl bg-paper">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.4rem,2.4vw,1.85rem)] leading-tight mb-4">Beyond the numbers</h2>
        <p class="prose-body">
          Traditional polling tells us what people believe, but not why. By listening closely, we
          uncover the experiences, emotions, and identities that shape opinions &mdash; helping move
          beyond checkbox questions and into the rich, human context that drives belief.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="p-8 md:p-10 rounded-2xl bg-paper">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.4rem,2.4vw,1.85rem)] leading-tight mb-4">Breaking the binary</h2>
        <p class="prose-body">
          Too often, public conversation is framed by partisan extremes. Our method reveals
          perspectives that don&rsquo;t fit neatly into &ldquo;left&rdquo; or &ldquo;right&rdquo; &mdash; the mixed feelings,
          contradictions, and thoughtful nuance that define real communities. This clarity is
          essential in a world shaped by complexity, not just ideology.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="p-8 md:p-10 rounded-2xl bg-paper md:col-span-2">
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-12 gap-6 md:gap-10 items-start">
          <div class="md:col-span-5">
            <h2 class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.4rem,2.4vw,1.85rem)] leading-tight">Centering people</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="md:col-span-7">
            <p class="prose-body">
              People share their stories with us not just to be heard, but to shape a better world
              &mdash; for themselves, their families, and their neighbors. We conduct interviews in many
              languages, across diverse communities, with empathy and respect at the core. The result
              is a more accurate and inclusive picture of what people care about &mdash; one that informs
              smarter decisions, better storytelling, and more human engagement.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

  
  <section class="container-site mt-16">
    <div class="border-l-2 border-terracotta pl-8 md:pl-12 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="font-serif text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.6vw,2rem)] leading-[1.25] text-ink">
        Polls tell you the score. They don&rsquo;t tell you the game.
      </p>
      <p class="prose-body mt-6">
        A poll can tell you 58% of voters in a district support a policy &mdash; but not whether that
        support is deep or shallow, what experiences shaped it, or how it connects to identity
        and community. Our method captures the texture that polls miss, with the statistical
        rigor they provide.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-site mt-20">
    <div class="border-t border-fog/40 pt-10 flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between gap-4">
      <p class="font-serif text-[22px] text-ink">Interested in what we&rsquo;re building?</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
